  "notes": [
    "the Windows volume on disk 0 partition 3, 300.0 GiB: Windows is hibernated on it, or was shut down with Fast Startup. The plan replaces it, so what Windows saved there (its open programs and files) is lost; the backup holds the volume whole. Start Windows and shut it down fully: hold Shift while you choose Shut down, or turn off Fast Startup (Control Panel, Power Options, Choose what the power buttons do, Change settings that are currently unavailable, untick Turn on fast startup) and then shut down. A hibernated Windows comes back to the state it saved, not to what is on the disk: writing next to it, or backing it up and restoring it, can lose data on that volume."
  ]
